L.RB_GM_HERALDRY_UNLOCKS = "Every kind of decree and the Agenda, for your guild only. The Heraldry room."
L.RB_GM_CHURCHDEPT = "Missionary Church correspondent (the Guild tab)"
L.RB_GM_CHURCHDEPT_JOB = "Your guild's Church contact: brings new players in and helps keep the guild full."
L.RB_GM_CHURCHDEPT_SHOWS = "The Missionary Church shield on his portrait and by his name."
L.RB_GM_CHURCHDEPT_UNLOCKS = "The title and the department room. The Church's own room and numbers come with the next line."
L.RB_GM_CHURCH = "Church correspondent (the Church tab)"
L.RB_GM_CHURCH_JOB = "Answers to the Head of the Church for keeping your guild full. Name the same person as above."
L.RB_GM_CHURCH_SHOWS = "Nothing on the portrait."
L.RB_GM_CHURCH_UNLOCKS = "The Church room, the Church tab's numbers, and registering recruits he brought."
L.RB_GM_BTN_CHURCH = "Open the Church"
L.RB_GM_WATCHERS = "Watchers"
L.RB_GM_WATCHERS_TEXT = "Your Council already have The Watch. Watchers get it too, for your members below them."
L.RB_GM_BTN_WATCHER = "Name a Watcher"
L.RB_GM_CHARTER = "Guild charter"
L.RB_GM_CHARTER_TEXT = "Purpose, language, raid nights and the classes you want, public for seven days. It helps recruits pick you."
L.RB_GM_BTN_WRITE = "Write it"
L.RB_GM_BANK = "Guild bank"
L.RB_GM_BANK_TEXT = "Open your guild bank once with the addon on: it takes a snapshot, never moves anything. You decide if the whole guild sees it."
L.RB_GM_BTN_OPEN = "Open"
L.RB_GM_GET = "What you get as guild master:\n- The bronze wings on your portrait, and the bronze mark by your name.\n- The Guild tab: this list, and every department's page.\n- Calls to Arms, Musters, royal decrees and Tabard inspections for your guild.\n- Your guild's Agenda, and Poll polls for your guild.\n- The Watch for your guild, with your Council.\n- The Guild Masters, Masters & Legates, Master & Legates and Master & Correspondents rooms."
L.RB_GM_CLOSE = "One rule: your power stops at your guild's door. Inside it, use it well.\n\nNow go build something. Let's go!"

-- 3. The High Council, and a paragraph for a councillor's department title.
L.RB_COUNCIL_TITLE = "The High Council"
L.RB_COUNCIL = "Okay, listen.\n\nYou're on the High Council now. That's huge. You don't grind this rank. You got picked. Don't make us regret it.\n\nThe job: run Bankai Guild with me. Judge, call the army, look after the place.\n\nWhat shows: the silver wings on your portrait, and the silver dragon before your name in chat. You can add an icon after it in My profile, Icons.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Royal decrees, Tabard inspections, Calls to Arms and Musters for the whole army.\n- The Watch: the council's reports, and a vote on every Judgment. I give the final word.\n- Up to 10 Bankai Guild moderators of your own.\n- Naming Apostles, and opening the Church's public ranking.\n- Naming Legates for the Shogun's guild, on the Throne.\n- The High Council room.\n\nOne rule: you act for Bankai Guild, not for your guild."
L.RB_COUNCIL_BADGE = "Your department's shield shows on your portrait too."
L.RB_COUNCIL_WAR = "You head War. In your own guild's War Room you count as an officer. Your department room has every guild's War correspondent in it."
L.RB_COUNCIL_TREASURY = "You head the Federal Treasury. Your department room has the Federal Treasurer and every guild's Treasury correspondent in it."
L.RB_COUNCIL_JUSTICE = "You sit on the Council of Justice. I preside it. When I'm not around, a High Councillor does. Your department room has every guild's Justice correspondent in it."
L.RB_COUNCIL_ARTISANRY = "You head Artisanry. Your department room has every guild's Artisanry correspondent in it. The department's own tools come later."
L.RB_COUNCIL_HERALDRY = "You head Heraldry. You post the Shogun's Agenda for the whole army. Your department room has every guild's Heraldry correspondent in it."
L.RB_COUNCIL_CHURCHDEPT = "You head the Church's department. Your department room has every guild's Church correspondent in it, and the Church tab's ranking is open to you."

-- 4. Steward.
L.RB_STEWARD_TITLE = "My Steward"
L.RB_STEWARD = "Hey,\n\nYou're my Steward now. That means when I'm not around, you're me. No pressure.\n\nThe job: keep the Throne running in my name.\n\nWhat shows: no new frame. Your power is on the Throne tab.\n\nWhat you get:\n- The Throne, acting for the Shogun: roll call, Royal Inspection, the Agenda, Poll, the gates.\n- Hands of your own. You name them, you take them back.\n- The treasury's switches and keepers, and the weekly dues amount.\n- Every kind of decree, for the whole army.\n- The Secretariat room, with me.\n\nWhat stays mine: my own Hands, the court, writs and pardons.\n\nOne rule: act like I'm watching. Because I will be."

-- 5. Hand.
L.RB_HAND_TITLE = "Hand of the Shogun"
L.RB_HAND = "Okay,\n\nI made you a Hand of the Shogun. That's a big deal. You use my tools, in my name.\n\nWhat shows: no new frame. The Throne tab opens for you.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Summon Elders: a roll call of every Elder and Council member online.\n- Royal Inspection: the army checks the tabards around them.\n- The Shogun's Agenda, and Poll polls.\n- The gates: where new recruits go.\n- Calls to Arms and Musters for the whole army.\n\nWhat stays mine: the Hands list, writs, the court and pardons.\n\nOne rule: don't spam the army. Every call you send pops up on everybody's screen."

-- 6. Federal Treasurer.
L.RB_TREASURER_TITLE = "The Federal Treasurer"
L.RB_TREASURER = "Hey,\n\nYou're the Federal Treasurer. You hold the gold of Bankai Guild. Yeah. All of it.\n\nThe job: keep the treasury honest, and in one book.\n\nWhat shows: the Treasurer's dragon frame on your portrait.\n\nWhat you get:\n- The Treasury tab and your book: every trade and mail with gold or items goes in by itself, once you say yes to sharing it.\n- The weekly dues, paid to you. Who paid stays private: the Shogun and each guild's Council see it, never the army.\n- The High Council room and the Federal Treasury room.\n\nWhat you earn playing is yours. It never goes in the book.\n\nOne rule: every copper in, every copper out. On the book."

-- 7. Treasury keeper.
L.RB_KEEPER_TITLE = "Keeper of the treasury"
L.RB_KEEPER = "Hey,\n\nI named you a keeper of the treasury. I trust you with the gold. Don't make it weird.\n\nThe job: hold part of the treasury on your character, alongside the Treasurer.\n\nWhat shows: no new frame.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Your own book on the Treasury tab. Gold and items people give you by trade or mail count as donations, by themselves, once you say yes to sharing it.\n- Gold between two keepers is a transfer, never a donation.\n- What you earn playing stays yours. A sale or a purchase goes in as not counted.\n\nThere are five keepers at most, and I can take it back any time.\n\nOne rule: donated gold is never yours to spend."

-- 8. Legate.
L.RB_LEGATE_TITLE = "Legate"
L.RB_LEGATE = "Okay, listen.\n\nYou're a Legate of <%s> now. Let's go!\n\nThe job: lead a raid group. You and up to 39 guildmates who agreed, 40 in all. Get them to events, raids and wars.\n\nWhat shows: the Legate shield on your portrait, and the same shield by your name.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Your group in the War Room (The Realm tab): assign and remove soldiers, invite the ones online to raid, a private squad chat.\n- The Masters & Legates rooms in Chat.\n\nNothing is automatic: no guild invite, kick or promotion. Groups are optional, and people can play with another leader.\n\nOne rule: only list people who said yes."

-- 9. The six department correspondents.
L.RB_CORR_TREASURY_TITLE = "Treasury correspondent"
L.RB_CORR_TREASURY = "Hey,\n\nYou're <%s>'s Treasury correspondent now. Nice.\n\nThe job: keep your guild's Treasury records and bank sharing in order, with your guild master and the Federal Treasury.\n\nWhat shows: the Federal Treasury shield on your portrait and by your name.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Your guild's bank in the addon. Open the guild bank with the addon on and it takes a snapshot. It never moves anything. Your guild master decides if the whole guild sees it.\n- The Federal Treasury room, and the Master & Correspondents room.\n\nOne rule: the guild's gold is the guild's. Keep the books clean."
L.RB_CORR_WAR_TITLE = "War correspondent"
L.RB_CORR_WAR = "Okay,\n\nYou're <%s>'s War correspondent now. You're the one who makes the raids happen.\n\nThe job: organize your guild's raids and PvP operations, its raid groups and after-action records.\n\nWhat shows: the Department of War shield on your portrait and by your name.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Officer rights in your guild's War Room (The Realm tab): operations, raid groups, posts, after-action records.\n- The Department of War room, and the Master & Correspondents room.\n\nAll of it inside your own guild.\n\nOne rule: plan it, call it, show up for it."
L.RB_CORR_JUSTICE_TITLE = "Justice correspondent"
L.RB_CORR_JUSTICE = "Hey,\n\nYou're <%s>'s Justice correspondent now. You keep the peace.\n\nThe job: watch your guild's chat, deal with problems, and work with your guild master and the Council of Justice.\n\nWhat shows: the Council of Justice shield on your portrait and by your name.\n\nWhat you get:\n- The whole Watch desk (The Watch tab) for your guild's members below you: warnings, timeouts, the watch list, reports.\n- When I uphold a case after the High Council votes, you apply it in your guild. The addon never kicks anyone by itself.\n- The Council of Justice room.\n\nOne rule: be fair. Same rules for your friends."
L.RB_CORR_ARTISANRY_TITLE = "Artisanry correspondent"
L.RB_CORR_ARTISANRY = "Hey,\n\nYou're <%s>'s Artisanry correspondent now. The crafters' best friend.\n\nThe job: help your guildmates find crafters, and get requests, mats and supplies to whoever needs them.\n\nWhat shows: the Association of Artisanry shield on your portrait and by your name.\n\nWhat you get:\n- The Crafters board, one click from your Guild tab.\n- The Association of Artisanry room, and the Master & Correspondents room.\n\nThe department's own tools aren't in yet. For now, you're the person people ask.\n\nOne rule: nobody in your guild stays stuck without a craft."
L.RB_CORR_HERALDRY_TITLE = "Heraldry correspondent"
L.RB_CORR_HERALDRY = "Okay,\n\nYou're <%s>'s Heraldry correspondent now. You're the voice of your guild.\n\nThe job: run your guild's decrees, Agenda and musters, and keep people showing up for events and streams.\n\nWhat shows: the Department of Heraldry shield on your portrait and by your name.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Every decree for your guild: Calls to Arms, Musters, royal decrees, Tabard inspections.\n- Your guild's Agenda.\n- The Department of Heraldry room, and the Master & Correspondents room.\n\nYour guild only. The whole army is the Crown's and the High Council's.\n\nOne rule: don't cry wolf. Call when it matters."
L.RB_CORR_CHURCHDEPT_TITLE = "Missionary Church correspondent"
L.RB_CORR_CHURCHDEPT = "Hey,\n\nYou're <%s>'s correspondent for the Missionary Church now.\n\nThe job: bring new players in, and help keep your guild full.\n\nWhat shows: the Missionary Church shield on your portrait and by your name.\n\nWhat you get: the title, and the department room. Honestly, that's it. It tells everyone who your guild's Church contact is.\n\nFor the Church's own room and recruiting numbers you need a Church place too. Your guild master names the Church correspondent on the Church tab, or an Apostle names you a missionary.\n\nOne rule: bring in real new players. Alts and moves between Bankai Guild guilds never count."

-- 10. The Church correspondent (the Church tab's place).
L.RB_CHURCHCORR_TITLE = "Church correspondent"
L.RB_CHURCHCORR = "Hey,\n\nYou're <%s>'s Church correspondent now. You answer to the Head of the Church. That's me.\n\nThe job: keep your guild full.\n\nWhat shows: no new frame.\n\nWhat you get:\n- The Church tab: the ranking, your own numbers, and the people.\n- Register a recruit you brought, up to 15 open at once. He counts for you if he joins an Bankai Guild guild within 14 days and is new to Bankai Guild.\n- The Church room in Chat.\n\nYour ranking is days in a row above 950 members, counted from your appointment.\n\nOne rule: grow your guild, but never by pulling people out of another Bankai Guild guild."

-- 11. Watcher.
L.RB_WATCHER_TITLE = "Watcher"
L.RB_WATCHER = "Hey,\n\nYour guild master named you a Watcher of <%s>. You help keep the chat clean.\n\nThe job: keep an eye on your guild's chat, and step in when somebody crosses the line.\n\nWhat shows: nothing on your portrait.\n\nWhat you get: the whole Watch desk (The Watch tab) for your guild's members below you: warnings, timeouts, the watch list, reports and cases.\n\nYou stay a Watcher while your guild master keeps you on his list.\n\nOne rule: warn first. Timeouts climb from there: an hour, a day, a week."

-- 12. Bankai Guild moderator.
L.RB_MODERATOR_TITLE = "Bankai Guild moderator"
L.RB_MODERATOR = "Okay, listen.\n\nYou're an Bankai Guild moderator now. You keep the chats of the whole army clean. That's a real job.\n\nThe job: deal with abuse, slurs, spam and scams in the Bankai Guild chats.\n\nWhat shows: nothing on your portrait.\n\nWhat you get:\n- The Watch's chat moderation: delete lines and time people out anywhere in Bankai Guild, other guild masters included. Never the master of <Elfcore>, or anyone above you.\n- The Watch room, with the High Council, the other moderators and me.\n\nYou keep it while the one who named you keeps you on his list.\n\nOne rule: what you see on the team stays on the team."

-- 13. Apostle, on being named (RB_APOSTLE_RED only for one who may wear the red cross).
L.RB_APOSTLE_TITLE = "Apostle"
L.RB_APOSTLE_1 = "Hey,\n\nYou're one of the Twelve Apostles of the Missionary Church of Bankai Guild now. Twelve. That's it. That's huge.\n\nThe job: bring new players into Bankai Guild, and build a network of missionaries who do the same.\n\nWhat shows: the top three Apostles of the last 30 days wear the Apostles' cross, and everybody sees it."
L.RB_APOSTLE_RED = "In My profile, under Look, there's also a red cross that only you see."
L.RB_APOSTLE_2 = "What you get:\n- Up to 12 missionaries of your own (Church tab, Name, or right-click a player).\n- The Church tab: the ranking, your numbers, the people.\n- The Apostles room and the Church rooms in Chat.\n- While you play, your addon keeps the Church's book for everyone.\n\nOne rule: name people who will actually do it."

-- 14. Every Apostle at launch.
L.RB_APOSTLE_LAUNCH_TITLE = "The Church, at launch"
L.RB_APOSTLE_LAUNCH = "Okay, listen.\n\nThe game is live. You're one of twelve Apostles in the whole army. That's huge. Now the Church earns its name.\n\nSame job: bring new players into Bankai Guild, and build missionaries who do the same.\n\n- Name missionaries: up to 12 each, on the Church tab (Name) or by right-clicking a player. They name their own, down to five levels below you. 5,000 in the whole Church, max.\n- Points: 10 for each player new to Bankai Guild who joins through you, 5 more if he's still here 7 days later. Plus 25%, 10% and 5% of what your three levels below bring in. Someone below you can outscore you. Good. It means it's working.\n- Brought someone another player invited? Register him: he counts if he joins an Bankai Guild guild within 14 days.\n- The top three Apostles of the last 30 days wear the cross.\n- Someone stopped playing? Remove him. The people he named keep their places.\n\nOne rule: real new players only. Alts and moves between Bankai Guild guilds never count. Points are in game only, never gold.\n\nKeep your addon on while you play. It keeps the Church's book. Let's go!"

-- 15. Missionary, on being named (%s: his network's Apostle, or the Head of the Church).
L.RB_MISSIONARY_TITLE = "Missionary"
L.RB_MISSIONARY = "Hey,\n\nYou're a missionary of the Church now, in %s's network. Welcome in.\n\nThe job: bring new players into Bankai Guild.\n\nWhat shows: the top three missionaries of the last 30 days wear the shepherd's crook.\n\nWhat you get:\n- Invite new players to your guild and the addon counts it by itself, once another player's addon confirms it.\n- Brought someone another player invited? Register him on the Church tab. He counts if he joins an Bankai Guild guild within 14 days.\n- Up to 12 missionaries of your own, unless you're already five levels down.\n- The Church tab, the Apostles & Missionaries room and the Church room.\n\nPoints: 10 for each new player, 5 more if he stays 7 days.\n\nOne rule: real new players only. Alts and moves between Bankai Guild guilds never count."

